Match the extensions-root override the way the file system would

The override path was compared to the known VS Code roots case-insensitively
everywhere, but only Windows and macOS have case-insensitive file systems. On
Linux ~/.VSCODE/extensions is a genuinely different directory, so a VSCodium
or custom-gallery build parked there was promoted to the Microsoft Marketplace
and got the outbound lookup this classification exists to prevent.

Also stops the disk-recovery comment from claiming more than it can. Version
equality rules out a copy in another extensions root, not a non-default
profile that side-loaded the same version -- profiles share the extracted
folder and keep their own metadata, and VS Code exposes no per-profile source
signal to close that gap.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
